  "rendered": {
    "title": "Smarter status investigations, calmer upgrade gate, and a self-healing desktop harness",
    "intro": "Today's nightly tightens how Aura's status system reasons about outages, stops the forced-upgrade overlay from interrupting active chats, prunes unavailable image and chat models, and teaches the desktop harness to clear out stale sidecars before launch.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "7:26 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-16T14:26:04.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-16T15:29:16.000Z",
        "title": "Status probe tuning and grounded investigations",
        "summary": "The observability pipeline got more tolerant freshness windows and a stricter, evidence-only investigator so root-cause writeups stop drifting into speculation.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Relaxed staleness and latency thresholds for API health, snapshot freshness, and the public website snapshot check, and shifted the scheduled observability cron off the hour to avoid runner contention — fewer false 'stale' or latency warnings on the public status surface.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5a0475f59638f66a335b31a10ea9c92a6e06ee49"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Raised the model-matrix runtime eval timeout from 45s to 120s (with matching warning/outage budgets up to 180s/360s) so cold model responses no longer trip the status check.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "2049590dd90f5d4c09d19b3cd141daa6d0a52c24"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "The status investigator is now constrained to cite only commits and paths that appear in the supplied evidence, with a sanitization pass that strips unsupported references from proof, causes, affected areas, and follow-up probes.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "2049590dd90f5d4c09d19b3cd141daa6d0a52c24",
              "7560151f6d3be0c6939c7f288a51398f71186182"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Source discovery now scores and prioritizes search needles (endpoints, error codes, multi-word phrases) and prefers product code paths over observability framework files, producing more focused suspect-change lists.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "7c8e0405beda70cdad1e6f405f3c9c168cde63db"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-2",
        "time_label": "8:52 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-16T15:52:02.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-16T15:52:02.000Z",
        "title": "Forced-upgrade overlay waits for the user to be idle",
        "summary": "The upgrade gate no longer interrupts an in-progress turn or extraction; it defers until the active stream finishes.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a global useIsAnyStreaming() selector and used it to defer the ForcedUpgradeOverlay latch while any stream is active. Once the user is idle the gate appears, and a stream starting after the gate is shown will not dismiss it — defer, not cancel.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "04c81439f3bc03beeddb426490521079d80efe56"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "10:56 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-16T17:56:04.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-16T18:08:13.000Z",
        "title": "Model catalog cleanup and retry-with-current-model",
        "summary": "Unavailable Fable and DALL-E entries were removed from the model picker, retries now use the model you have selected today, and project APIs preserve build/test commands across updates.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Dropped the unavailable Fable chat model and the DALL-E 2 / DALL-E 3 image models from the picker, defaults, ETA tables, and the whitepaper seed; stale persisted DALL-E selections now fall back to gpt-image-2 instead of staying stuck on a missing model.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "45b40a1b6ea09eca5f19adf4f3e9f0cded83de65",
              "0017da2fa7e298c15eaddc462106a0ac5aed6ab9"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Retrying a failed chat turn now uses the currently selected model rather than the cached model that originally failed, so swapping away from a broken model and hitting Retry actually re-runs against the new one.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fa001c127b0ec77c956560a3cfeed2b7cbbcb723"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Project create and update requests now carry build_command and test_command, and the server preserves them across PUT/GET round-trips so tooling metadata no longer gets dropped on edit.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "65d4bede047c6dd234d12736dde9515f5d5dede2"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-4",
        "time_label": "1:48 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-16T20:48:48.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-16T20:48:48.000Z",
        "title": "Desktop harness reclaims its port from stale sidecars",
        "summary": "On Unix, the desktop app now detects and terminates orphaned managed harness sidecars holding the local port before spawning a fresh one.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Before launching the local harness, the desktop sidecar manager uses lsof to find processes listening on the harness port, classifies them as the current expected binary or a stale managed sidecar under runtime/sidecar, and terminates stale ones so the new harness can bind cleanly instead of failing health probes.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "d44c39d97f710d17e094f3c793ea6bca937e5af2"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
